 "caption": "Full-text access by publisher for the eligible 2022 papers of round 1 and round 2. (a, c) Each bar splits a publisher's eligible papers into PDF and XML, PDF only, XML only, and no full text. XML is publisher full-text XML with the article body: JATS (Journal Article Tag Suite, the standard XML for articles) for Copernicus, Springer and Nature Portfolio papers, and Elsevier article XML from the Elsevier full-text API (74 of 79 Elsevier papers in round 1, 29 of 31 Elsevier papers in round 2); Elsevier full-text XML requests were refused (HTTP 403) for 1 of 31 Elsevier papers in round 2. The number after the publisher name is its eligible count; the fraction at the right (\"any full text\") counts papers with a PDF or XML. (b, d) Share of the same papers that OpenAlex lists as open access. Publisher is the OpenAlex host organization, not the DOI registrant, with two exceptions: papers whose journal is on the AGU journal list are shown as AGU (Wiley), which in these rounds are exactly the papers with DOI prefix 10.1029, and papers with DOI prefix 10.5194 (European Journal of Mineralogy, hosted by OpenAlex under Elsevier) are shown as Copernicus. GJI, SRL and BSSA are shown by journal; their publishers are given in parentheses. Springer joins the two OpenAlex labels Springer and Springer Nature (Nature Portfolio is shown apart) and includes Pleiades translations of Russian journals (DOI prefixes 10.1134 and 10.3103; 55 of 110 papers in round 1, 5 of 57 papers in round 2); the Elsevier host includes 4 GeoScienceWorld (10.2113) and 1 Wiley (10.1002) DOIs in round 1, and 1 GeoScienceWorld (10.2113) DOI in round 2. Publishers with fewer than 5 eligible papers in a round are pooled as Other (round 1: Science Advances 1, Seismica 1; round 2: BSSA 4, GJI 4, Science Advances 4, Seismica 4, SRL 2). Rows keep the round-1 order in both rounds. PDF status from the download queue and XML status from the round's xml_status.json, each confirmed on disk (queue as of 2026-10-27 08:29). Counts are a census of each eligible set, so no sampling interval is drawn. Round 1, n = 525: 188 PDF and XML, 191 PDF only, 2 XML only, 144 none; 328 open access. Round 2, n = 222: 134 PDF and XML, 68 PDF only, 0 XML only, 20 none; 222 open access. Round 2 was drawn from open-access papers only, with at most 4 papers per journal and a round robin over publishers (g18_round2_draw.py, seed 2027), so its publisher mix and its open-access share (1 for every publisher) are set by the design; its per-publisher shares are not a second sample of the round-1 population."
